  "notes": [
    "The new guard precedes shared vector/read_f32 calls and weight payload loading. It adds no execution arithmetic, callback/lifetime change or allocation-heavy operation.",
    "Every active BERT normalization weight/bias and optional attention/FFN bias matches the guard. The pre-existing F32 token-type table guard is preserved.",
    "The frozen build_pooling classifier branch applies cls_b only inside if(cls), and cls_out_b only inside if(cls_out). The two explicit name exceptions correctly allow decodable unpaired classifier biases.",
    "Both original compiler profiles independently abort all five active F16/BF16 cases at binary_op with F32 destination/left operand and half-precision right operand. Both controls and both unpaired-bias cases execute successfully.",
    "The test explicitly translates native process aborts to checked Rust loader errors and checks the source binary-graph diagnostic. It replays full native observations for the four successful cases. A source process abort is not represented here as an original model-load rejection.",
    "The model-level rule also rejects a paired half-precision classifier bias when a future context would select ordinary pooling. This is a deliberate narrower admission scope, stated in ENCODER.md and fixture provenance; it is not claimed as exact context-dependent native admission.",
    "The original primary 192-case corpus and its numerical tolerances are unchanged. This addendum was captured after the main implementation and sealed before the guard, as explicitly qualified in the provenance."
  ],
